{
 "about": "Hand audit of typed relations (scripts/build_typed_relations.py), one reviewer who is also the author of the extractor, so not independent. precision: every extracted relation was read in context and judged (correct = the sentence states that relation between those two concepts). The first version extracted 88 relations of which 71 were correct (80.7%); the patterns were then tightened using exactly those errors, so the figure after tightening is optimistic: it was measured on the same sentences it was tuned on. recall: 66 sentences drawn at random from the sentences that name a fitting pair of concepts (22 for each of three relation types; CAUSES had no candidate sentences under the pair definition used), judged for whether a relation of that type is stated, then checked against what was extracted. The sample is small; treat the recall as rough.",
